# Tutorial fixture for example 2.5 (stb-defect): magnetite (Fe3O4),
# rhombohedral primitive cell (14 atoms), built from its space group
# (Fd-3m, No. 227) via pymatgen's Structure.from_spacegroup, with Fe at
# 8a/16d (no free parameter) and O at 32e (oxygen positional parameter
# u = 0.379, origin choice 2; a = 8.396 Ang). Approximate/illustrative
# values (not re-verified against a primary crystallographic reference) --
# fine for exercising code paths, don't use for production DFT without
# checking a proper source first.
#
# Chosen specifically because Fe sits on *two* symmetrically distinct
# sites -- tetrahedral 8a-type and octahedral 16d-type in the conventional
# cell (labeled 'a'/'d' in this primitive setting) -- while O is a single
# site: the textbook example of "same element, different Wyckoff class,
# different local environment, different defect formation energy." Used
# to exercise --all-inequivalent-sites (2 Fe sites found, multiplicities 2
# and 4; 1 O site, multiplicity 8) and --ml-rank (site #1, tetrahedral,
# ranks ~0.06 eV less stable than site #5, octahedral, for a Fe vacancy --
# a physically sensible, non-degenerate result, verified live).

NumberOfSpecies    2
NumberofAtoms      14

%block ChemicalSpeciesLabel
 1   26   Fe
 2   8   O
%endblock ChemicalSpeciesLabel

LatticeConstant 1.0 Ang

AtomicCoordinatesFormat  Fractional

%block LatticeVectors
 0.00000000   4.19800000   4.19800000
 4.19800000   0.00000000   4.19800000
 4.19800000   4.19800000   0.00000000
%endblock LatticeVectors

%block AtomicCoordinatesAndAtomicSpecies
  0.12500000   0.62500000   0.12500000   1
  0.62500000   0.12500000   0.12500000   1
  0.12500000   0.12500000   0.62500000   1
  0.12500000   0.12500000   0.12500000   1
  0.50000000   0.50000000   0.50000000   1
  0.75000000   0.75000000   0.75000000   1
  0.37900000   0.86300000   0.37900000   2
  0.38700000   0.87100000   0.87100000   2
  0.37900000   0.37900000   0.86300000   2
  0.87100000   0.38700000   0.87100000   2
  0.37900000   0.37900000   0.37900000   2
  0.87100000   0.87100000   0.87100000   2
  0.86300000   0.37900000   0.37900000   2
  0.87100000   0.87100000   0.38700000   2
%endblock AtomicCoordinatesAndAtomicSpecies
